---
title: Summoning actors
sidebar:
  order: 8
---

Actors can summon other actors during battle. Magikoopa uses this to make clones, and Bill Blaster uses it to fire Bullet Bills.

## SummonEnemy

Use `SummonEnemy` to summon an actor from a formation in the summoner's file. `SummonEnemy` spawns the actor in the formation's first row, and ignores any other rows. It waits for the summoned actor's `EVS_Init` to finish, and then puts the actor's ID in `LVar0`.

```c
Formation CloneFormation = {
    OVL_ACTOR_BY_IDX("frost_goomba", BTL_POS_GROUND_C, 10),
};

EvtScript EVS_TakeTurn = {
    // ...
    Call(SummonEnemy, Ref(CloneFormation), false)
    // LVar0 holds the new actor's ID
    // ...
};
```

The second argument is `true` to put the summoned actor last in the turn order. Most actors pass `false`.

To summon more than one actor, call `SummonEnemy` once for each, with a formation for each.

## Storing the summoned actor's ID

To refer to the summoned actor later, save its ID in an [actor variable](/papermario-dx/battles/actors/actor-variables/):

```c
enum ActorVars {
    AVAR_SpawnedActorID = 0,
};

EvtScript EVS_TakeTurn = {
    // ...
    Call(SummonEnemy, Ref(CloneFormation), false)
    Call(SetActorVar,
        ACTOR_SELF, AVAR_SpawnedActorID, LVar0)
    // ...
};
```

## Passing data to summoned actors

The summoned actor's `EVS_Init` runs before `SummonEnemy` returns, so it can't see variables you set after summoning. To give it values that `EVS_Init` reads, set them in the formation's `.var0`, `.var1`, `.var2`, and `.var3` fields, which become the actor's variables 0 to 3:

```c
Formation CloneFormation = {
    OVL_ACTOR_BY_IDX("frost_goomba", BTL_POS_GROUND_C, 10, .var0 = true),
};
```

If a value is only known at runtime, such as the summoner's actor ID, write it to the formation from C before summoning. Bill Blaster does this with an API function, so each Bullet Bill knows which blaster fired it:

```c
API_CALLABLE(SetBulletInitVars) {
    BulletFormation[0].var0 = true;
    BulletFormation[0].var1 = script->owner1.actorID;

    return ApiStatus_DONE2;
}

EvtScript EVS_Move_FireBullet = {
    // ...
    Call(SetBulletInitVars)
    Call(SummonEnemy, Ref(BulletFormation), false)
    // ...
};
```

If the summoned actor reads a variable only after `EVS_Init`, such as in its `EVS_TakeTurn`, you can also set it with `SetActorVar` after summoning, using the ID in `LVar0`.

For more on variables, see [Actor variables](/papermario-dx/battles/actors/actor-variables/).

For complete examples, see `battle/actor/magikoopa.c` (cloning) and `battle/actor/bill_blaster.c` (summoning projectiles).
